Z||000000||MooCow||06-07-2001||07:59 AM||||I am so happy right now.  I got my Fiero on a Semi to get fixed at Ed Parks Fiero Factory on Monday and it is already fixed.  This is what said:Ken, the car was driven home tonight (as a final test) by Dave, the<BR>technician that I had working on it (and originally installed the 3.4).<BR>He has a 3.4 in his 87 5 spd GT, but was VERY impressed with yours w/4.10<BR>4 spd. Said the test drive was much quicker then his. So QUICK, he<BR>smelled the brakes when he HAD to slow down for traffic.<P>Thankfully, the oil pressure is still outstanding, despite the abuse of<BR>fuel dilution. Good, tough, engine, no smoke, and FAST, in spite of<BR>you/others trying to ruin it!!! <P>You can come for it at anytime, but please, contact me FIRST if you have<BR>any other problems with your14 yr old Fiero. <P>Bendix was bad on the starter. Put on a good used starter. No more<BR>ZZZZZZ.<P>Hmmm, maybe I'll "test" drive it until you arrive!!!! Sorta miss my 4.10<BR>since I made the mistake of converting my 3.4 to a 5 spd and now don't<BR>have the time to change back!!!<P>If anything is changed by tomorrow, will let you know.<P>I am so happy.  Now all I have to do is find a way to bring it back home.  I tell you I hate all the mechanics around here.  Everyone wanted to charge me around $700 to replace the headgaskets and it wasn't even the problem.<P>                                 Thanks Ken<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig.jpg"> <BR>87 GT, 3.4 engine with a 4:10 tranny, and Viper Yellow!||||reg||12
